      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.76,
      "end": 2.38,
      "text": "Hello, how are things going?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 8.96,
      "end": 16.19,
      "text": "Gluten free bread is a different beast, but you can get something good. Start with a flour blend that already contains xanthan gum or psyllium."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 18.88,
      "end": 25.06,
      "text": "It acts a bit like gluten, holding the dough together and trapping air. Bread made with it is far less crumbly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 32.87,
      "end": 39.47,
      "text": "Yes, gluten free dough is usually much wetter. Don't add more flour to make it feel like normal dough, it'll come out dry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 42.71,
      "end": 49.87,
      "text": "Bake it in a covered pot for the first part, then uncover it. And let it cool fully before slicing, it finishes setting as it cools."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 54.44,
      "end": 57.23,
      "text": "It really is. Warm bread smells unfair."
    }
  ]
